<title>UK: BSE cases in UK fall 56 pct in year to June.</title>
<headline>BSE cases in UK fall 56 pct in year to June.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Clinically suspect cases of Bovine Spongiform Encephalopathy (mad cow disease) fell 56 percent in the year ended last June on a year earlier, Agriculture Minister Jack Cunningham said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>&quot;A continued improvement is expected for the future,&quot; he said in a parliamentary written answer which did not give the total number of cases.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7767</p>
</text>
